<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balj ibn Bishr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 742</span> · Also known as Balj ibn Bishr al-Qushayri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balj ibn Bishr al-Qushayri was an Arab commander who led Syrian troops sent to crush the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> revolt of 740 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. After their defeat he crossed with the survivors to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> in 741, helped suppress the Berbers there and then seized power as governor. He was killed in 742 fighting the established Arab settlers, and his Syrian troops were later settled in military districts in the south.</p></div>
